1
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:11,260
Boom!

2
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:16,516
At the buzzer, Wayne "Captain Clutch"
Rigsby nails the 3.

3
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:18,643
And the crowd goes insane.

4
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:23,564
I hate the night shift.

5
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,150
Hey, Jane. Teach me
a card trick, will ya?

6
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:33,241
Card trick?

7
00:00:39,121 --> 00:00:40,540
- Say, "pick a card".
- Okay.

8
00:00:43,876 --> 00:00:44,919
Pick a card.

9
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:50,591
Okay.
Put it back in the deck.

10
00:00:53,177 --> 00:00:55,638
Place the deck very gently
on your forehead.

11
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:58,849
Now try to visualize
the card that I picked, hmm?

12
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:01,602
Just focus and see it.

13
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:04,689
- What springs to mind?
- Um, the, uh...

14
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:07,483
- What card do you see?
- Nine of hearts.

15
00:01:08,609 --> 00:01:09,652
Nine of hearts.

16
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:11,862
Oh.

17
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:15,825
- That it?
- Huh. How'd I do that?

18
00:01:16,492 --> 00:01:17,535
Very good.

19
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:18,744
Very, very good.

20
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:21,872
- Let me try.
- All right.

21
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:24,625
Pick a card.

22
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:27,461
Now...

23
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:29,755
memorize it.

24
00:01:36,637 --> 00:01:38,055
- Jack of diamonds.
- Nope.

25
00:01:39,515 --> 00:01:40,558
Mm?

26
00:01:42,226 --> 00:01:43,352
- Are you sure?
- Yep.

27
00:01:43,769 --> 00:01:46,564
- Well, uh, Cho...
- It's a card trick. Not interested.

28
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:50,901
- Well, I guess card tricks are lame.
-Yep, when they don't work.

29
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:53,738
We're up.

30
00:02:09,545 --> 00:02:10,588
What do you think, doc?

31
00:02:11,088 --> 00:02:14,383
Your basic blunt force trauma.
Baseball bat type of deal.

32
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:16,510
- Mugging gone wrong, maybe?
- Don't think so.

33
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:18,471
His wallet's gone
but he did have this on him.

34
00:02:18,971 --> 00:02:20,890
It was wrapped in a napkin
with a note written on it.

35
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:25,645
Eh, the mysterious case
of the jilted jockey.

36
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:26,896
Don't be flippant.

37
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:29,565
- You think he's a jockey?
- Oh, I know he is.

38
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:31,984
- Why, because he's small?
- Small, bowlegged...

39
00:02:32,151 --> 00:02:33,903
Hungry-thin
in a thousand dollar jacket

40
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:35,488
deep tan from working outdoors

41
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:37,114
raccoon eyes
from wearing goggles.

42
00:02:37,239 --> 00:02:38,991
And that is a horseshoe on that napkin

43
00:02:39,116 --> 00:02:42,828
probably from a-a bar in town
that has "horseshoe" in the name.

44
00:02:42,953 --> 00:02:44,246
Well, he could be
a racecar driver.

45
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:46,374
Racecar drivers have soft hands.

46
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:47,958
Why a jilted jockey?

47
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:50,711
Because it alliterates it
and that is always a little fun.

48
00:02:50,878 --> 00:02:52,797
And who else but a forsaken lover

49
00:02:52,922 --> 00:02:55,299
would ask for forgiveness
on a cocktail napkin?

50
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:57,051
With a ring, no less.

51
00:02:57,968 --> 00:02:59,553
Golden Horseshoe Restaurant
about a mile away.

52
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,806
- "Here you go."
- Sorry, agents, wait.

53
00:03:02,264 --> 00:03:04,433
I just found this
in John Doe's jacket pockets.

54
00:03:04,934 --> 00:03:06,519
I don't know why
I didn't notice it before.

55
00:03:07,978 --> 00:03:09,021
Thanks.

56
00:03:09,146 --> 00:03:11,649
I figure it's some kinda message
maybe from the killer.

57
00:03:11,857 --> 00:03:13,359
That's my card.
How did you do that?

58
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:15,069
Huh? What?

59
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:17,238
Card tricks?

60
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:19,156
A man has lost his life.

61
00:03:19,448 --> 00:03:20,825
You should be ashamed
of yourself.

62
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:25,871
- Shame.
- Never mind.

63
00:03:25,996 --> 00:03:29,458
Shame. Shame.
So shameful. Terrible.

64
00:03:46,056 --> 00:03:47,808
Flashy clothes about 5'5",
skinny...

65
00:03:48,016 --> 00:03:49,184
like maybe
he could be a jockey.

66
00:03:50,644 --> 00:03:53,439
Sounds like Bill Button.
No, it's... Sutton.

67
00:03:53,772 --> 00:03:54,815
That's the name.

68
00:03:55,274 --> 00:03:56,734
He used to date Delinda...

69
00:03:57,025 --> 00:03:58,694
girl who works here
as a hostess.

70
00:03:59,111 --> 00:04:00,696
He came in last night
looking for her

71
00:04:00,863 --> 00:04:02,030
had a couple of drinks.

72
00:04:02,573 --> 00:04:05,951
Tried to leave something for her
but I told him I couldn't accept it.

73
00:04:06,827 --> 00:04:07,870
Policy.

74
00:04:08,245 --> 00:04:09,288
{\an8}Did you see what it was?

75
00:04:10,456 --> 00:04:13,500
{\an8}Yeah. It was a ring
with a note on a napkin.

76
00:04:14,042 --> 00:04:15,085
{\an8}"Forgive me".

77
00:04:16,003 --> 00:04:17,045
{\an8}Forgive him for what?
Do you know?

78
00:04:17,296 --> 00:04:19,256
Men. It was always something.

79
00:04:20,758 --> 00:04:22,634
{\an8}- So what's happened to him?
- Well, he's dead.

80
00:04:22,801 --> 00:04:24,887
{\an8}The girlfriend... Delinda.
What's her full name?

81
00:04:26,972 --> 00:04:28,015
Um...

82
00:04:28,432 --> 00:04:30,142
{\an8}It's... Lecure.

83
00:04:31,018 --> 00:04:32,102
{\an8}Delinda Lecure.

84
00:04:32,394 --> 00:04:33,604
She wasn't working
last night?

85
00:04:35,063 --> 00:04:36,815
No. He... he kept...

86
00:04:37,232 --> 00:04:39,276
coming in, hassling her
to get back together with him.

87
00:04:39,526 --> 00:04:41,570
So she started switching shifts
to avoid him.

88
00:04:41,904 --> 00:04:42,946
He get heavy with her?

89
00:04:43,822 --> 00:04:44,865
Physical.

90
00:04:44,990 --> 00:04:47,534
{\an8}No. No, no. He was always
a gentleman... what I saw.

91
00:04:47,701 --> 00:04:49,787
{\an8}But I-I stay out of that stuff.
You know...

92
00:04:50,579 --> 00:04:52,831
{\an8}- TMI.
- She have any other boyfriends?

93
00:04:53,081 --> 00:04:54,166
Anyone else interested?

94
00:04:54,875 --> 00:04:55,918
Not that I know of.

95
00:04:56,043 --> 00:04:58,670
{\an8}- You have an address for Delinda?
- Yeah, I-I got it here somewhere.

96
00:05:05,677 --> 00:05:08,430
{\an8}Cho and Rigsby are talking
to the ex-girlfriend, Delinda, now.

97
00:05:08,639 --> 00:05:09,681
{\an8}Anything else on the victim?

98
00:05:09,807 --> 00:05:12,059
{\an8}A William Q. Sutton
is scheduled to ride a horse

99
00:05:12,184 --> 00:05:13,936
{\an8}in for fifth race
at Redwood Downs today.

100
00:05:14,353 --> 00:05:15,646
{\an8}- So he is a jockey.
- Yep.

101
00:05:15,771 --> 00:05:17,731
Riding for a man
named Cobb Holwell.

102
00:05:19,149 --> 00:05:21,527
{\an8}Jane, we're going to Redwood Downs.

103
00:05:22,027 --> 00:05:24,279
{\an8}Yeah, yeah, you were right.
He's a jockey.

104
00:05:24,404 --> 00:05:26,615
{\an8}- You coming or not?
- I grew up around horses.

105
00:05:26,782 --> 00:05:29,117
{\an8}Fine. You can drive.
I'll meet you out there.

106
00:05:29,243 --> 00:05:30,619
{\an8}- I could come with.
- See what you can find out

107
00:05:30,744 --> 00:05:32,538
{\an8}about this Cobb Holwell, okay?

108
00:05:49,888 --> 00:05:52,599
{\an8}Why does horse manure
smell so good?

109
00:05:53,016 --> 00:05:54,059
{\an8}It doesn't.

110
00:05:56,311 --> 00:05:57,354
Excuse me.

111
00:05:59,314 --> 00:06:01,024
{\an8}You seen Cobb Holwell
around here?

112
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:02,943
You're here about Bill, huh?

113
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:05,279
Yeah. We're with the CBI.
We just have a couple questions.

114
00:06:05,654 --> 00:06:07,239
- And you are...
- Sam Starks.

115
00:06:08,031 --> 00:06:09,700
I'm an apprentice for Mr. Holwell.

116
00:06:11,076 --> 00:06:12,619
Nice animal.
What's his name?

117
00:06:13,453 --> 00:06:14,496
Castor's Folly.

118
00:06:14,788 --> 00:06:17,165
{\an8}Ah, yes. Castor's Folly.

119
00:06:17,291 --> 00:06:19,042
Sutton was gonna ride him
in the fifth race.

120
00:06:20,335 --> 00:06:21,837
Bill was so good with Cass.

121
00:06:23,213 --> 00:06:24,381
They had a deep bond.

122
00:06:27,384 --> 00:06:28,427
Poor soul.

123
00:06:29,511 --> 00:06:31,805
- He's grieving deeply.
- Aw.

124
00:06:32,014 --> 00:06:33,056
How do you know that?

125
00:06:34,266 --> 00:06:36,602
He knew something was wrong
so I told him.

126
00:06:38,770 --> 00:06:39,813
Okay.

127
00:06:40,606 --> 00:06:41,732
What happened to Bill?

128
00:06:41,899 --> 00:06:43,692
No idea yet.
What's your guess?

129
00:06:44,693 --> 00:06:45,736
I don't know.

130
00:06:46,111 --> 00:06:48,280
You think Cass might have
some kind of idea?

131
00:06:48,405 --> 00:06:50,240
Because we're pretty sure
Mr. Sutton's death

132
00:06:50,365 --> 00:06:51,825
had something to do with horses.

133
00:06:51,992 --> 00:06:53,827
Excuse me.
Cass has to finish his ride.

134
00:06:54,161 --> 00:06:56,455
You can find Mr. Holwell's stables
over there to the left.

135
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:02,044
Nice.
Teasing a grieving girl.

136
00:07:02,878 --> 00:07:05,547
Prodding, not teasing.
She could be the culprit...

137
00:07:06,089 --> 00:07:08,008
fiendish killer for all we know.

138
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:11,053
"Hell of a thing."

139
00:07:11,803 --> 00:07:12,888
"Bill was a good man."

140
00:07:14,848 --> 00:07:16,141
- "A good jock."
- Mr. Holwell

141
00:07:16,266 --> 00:07:18,393
uh, did Sutton have
any problems with anyone here?

142
00:07:18,936 --> 00:07:20,062
No. Well liked.

143
00:07:20,812 --> 00:07:21,855
How about women?

144
00:07:22,314 --> 00:07:23,398
Nothing I heard about.

145
00:07:24,149 --> 00:07:25,651
- Well, how long did he...
- Could he have won?

146
00:07:26,610 --> 00:07:28,153
Castor's Folly in the fifth race...

147
00:07:28,570 --> 00:07:29,905
did he have any chance
of winning?

148
00:07:30,197 --> 00:07:32,699
Always.
There's always a chance.

149
00:07:33,325 --> 00:07:35,702
Cass broke his maiden
by three lengths.

150
00:07:36,536 --> 00:07:39,081
Some problems since
but he's finding his form.

151
00:07:39,539 --> 00:07:40,582
He coulda won.

152
00:07:41,583 --> 00:07:44,378
Damn it. He woulda won.
Uh, never mind.

153
00:07:44,962 --> 00:07:46,213
There'll be another race.

154
00:07:47,089 --> 00:07:48,298
We'll find another jock.

155
00:07:48,465 --> 00:07:50,717
- How long did he work for you?
- About three weeks.

156
00:07:51,009 --> 00:07:53,720
- That's all?
- Oh, I'd known Bill for years.

157
00:07:54,638 --> 00:07:56,264
He'd been out of the game
for a while.

158
00:07:56,431 --> 00:07:58,225
When he came back
I hired him but quick.

159
00:07:58,934 --> 00:08:01,019
Gave him 20 grand to ride
for me exclusive.

160
00:08:01,478 --> 00:08:03,522
One final question...
where were you last night?

161
00:08:04,272 --> 00:08:06,358
- Here at the stable.
- All night?

162
00:08:06,858 --> 00:08:10,195
Ma'am, I am
the last independent stable

163
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:11,405
in this part of the state.

164
00:08:11,655 --> 00:08:14,616
I got one decent horse
and a hundred creditors.

165
00:08:14,741 --> 00:08:15,909
I don't sleep much.

166
00:08:16,118 --> 00:08:18,912
Jane, do you have any... questions.

167
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,123
Thanks for your time.

168
00:08:35,804 --> 00:08:38,015
Black blizzard in the sixth.
It's a lock, trust me.

169
00:08:38,849 --> 00:08:39,933
And where's that tip from?

170
00:08:40,684 --> 00:08:41,727
Somebody who knows.

171
00:08:42,728 --> 00:08:44,396
What are you, a race track cop?

172
00:08:44,855 --> 00:08:45,897
Does it seem legit?

173
00:08:46,356 --> 00:08:48,400
He's a groom at the track stable.
Sounds pretty good.

174
00:08:48,525 --> 00:08:50,652
He works around horses.
I guess he might know something.

175
00:08:50,819 --> 00:08:52,070
You betcha.
I got all the inside poop.

176
00:08:52,195 --> 00:08:54,197
20 bucks buys you a lock
in the 6th. A lock.

177
00:08:55,532 --> 00:08:56,575
How much you betting?

178
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,827
Well, you said it's a lock.
How much are you betting?

179
00:09:01,371 --> 00:09:04,249
All that poop inside, and you're outside
hustling for lunch money, huh?

180
00:09:04,374 --> 00:09:05,417
I'm trying to make a living
here, guy.

181
00:09:05,584 --> 00:09:07,544
- Move right along, why don't ya?
- You used to ride, didn't ya?

182
00:09:07,669 --> 00:09:09,296
Did you... did you know Bill Sutton?

183
00:09:11,089 --> 00:09:12,215
So you are a cop.

184
00:09:13,467 --> 00:09:14,509
You don't look like one.

185
00:09:15,135 --> 00:09:17,054
Yeah, I knew Sutton, and I'll say it
even though he's dead.

186
00:09:17,179 --> 00:09:18,388
He was a lowdown cheat.

187
00:09:19,639 --> 00:09:21,183
Now walk away, pal. I'm trying
to work with my friend here.

188
00:09:21,308 --> 00:09:24,269
Save your money. I'm a better judge
of horses than mister, uh...

189
00:09:24,394 --> 00:09:26,813
Ellis Barnes. Screw you.

190
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:28,940
Patrick Jane.
Nice to meet you, too.

191
00:09:29,858 --> 00:09:35,405
I will bet you that I can pick
first, second, and third horse

192
00:09:35,781 --> 00:09:38,533
any race you choose, Mr. Barnes
and you're my witness.

193
00:09:38,950 --> 00:09:41,119
Next race.
500 bucks says you can't.

194
00:09:43,455 --> 00:09:45,332
See you at the pay-out window
after the race.

195
00:09:53,423 --> 00:09:55,175
{\an8}Delinda Lecure, apartment 28.

196
00:09:56,885 --> 00:09:58,095
Why would anyone date
a jockey?

197
00:09:58,386 --> 00:09:59,930
Hungry little guy
smells like horses.

198
00:10:00,138 --> 00:10:01,181
Don't like horses?

199
00:10:01,389 --> 00:10:02,849
They're like dogs but bigger.

200
00:10:03,475 --> 00:10:04,518
You don't like dogs?

201
00:10:04,935 --> 00:10:06,978
It's all an act with dogs.
They do it for the food.

202
00:10:08,146 --> 00:10:09,189
Everybody does.

203
00:10:09,856 --> 00:10:10,899
That's deep.

204
00:10:12,692 --> 00:10:13,735
Ma'am?

205
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:15,654
"We're from the California Bureau
of Investigation"

206
00:10:16,238 --> 00:10:17,280
and we'd like to...

207
00:10:19,950 --> 00:10:21,159
Excuse me, ma'am.
Do you live here?

208
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,581
Oh, no, not today!

209
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,002
Hello?

210
00:10:33,213 --> 00:10:34,256
Hello?

211
00:10:54,776 --> 00:10:56,111
This is so ridiculous.

212
00:10:56,945 --> 00:10:58,405
- I don't understand.
- Take it easy.

213
00:10:58,530 --> 00:11:01,575
Hey, just get off me! Okay?
I have my rights.

214
00:11:01,992 --> 00:11:03,535
Hey, this is police brutality!

215
00:11:07,164 --> 00:11:08,290
- What are you gonna do?
- Hey!

216
00:11:09,332 --> 00:11:12,419
- Hey, what's going on?
- Hey, uh... Can you get me a lawyer?

217
00:11:12,586 --> 00:11:14,212
I kinda got this bench warrant
thing out on me.

218
00:11:14,379 --> 00:11:16,756
What bench warrant? We wanna
talk to you about your boyfriend.

219
00:11:17,132 --> 00:11:19,384
- What boyfriend?
- What bench warrant?

220
00:11:19,634 --> 00:11:20,969
Wait, are you talking
about Brandon?

221
00:11:21,094 --> 00:11:23,471
- 'Cause he is not my boyfriend.
- Are you Delinda Lecure?

222
00:11:23,805 --> 00:11:25,390
Nuh-unh. She is.

223
00:11:27,434 --> 00:11:28,727
Okay, who are you people?

224
00:11:35,942 --> 00:11:36,985
Where have you been?

225
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:39,196
Here, there.
Making new friends.

226
00:11:39,362 --> 00:11:40,822
I'll bet.
Come on. Let's go.

227
00:11:41,114 --> 00:11:42,157
One brief moment.

228
00:11:42,741 --> 00:11:45,785
In 25 seconds, come over
and insist I must leave immediately.

229
00:11:45,911 --> 00:11:47,495
What? Jane...

230
00:11:50,165 --> 00:11:51,374
One, two, three.

231
00:11:52,125 --> 00:11:54,127
One, two, three.
He did it.

232
00:11:54,336 --> 00:11:56,004
- Do it again.
- Some other time.

233
00:11:56,463 --> 00:11:57,797
- How much did you bet?
- 50.

234
00:11:58,048 --> 00:12:00,592
- 50 large?
- No. 50 cents.

235
00:12:02,469 --> 00:12:04,512
- Jane, let's go. Now.
- I won the trifecta.

236
00:12:04,638 --> 00:12:07,015
- I got a little cash to collect.
- Cool. Go ahead then.

237
00:12:07,390 --> 00:12:08,850
- We have plenty of time.
- Okay.

238
00:12:09,142 --> 00:12:10,685
I'm kidding. Come on.
Let's go.

239
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,313
Cough up.

240
00:12:15,732 --> 00:12:16,775
Thank you.

241
00:12:18,443 --> 00:12:19,486
Bye.

242
00:12:22,447 --> 00:12:23,698
Do I wanna know
what that was about?

243
00:12:23,865 --> 00:12:24,908
Uh, no.

244
00:12:25,450 --> 00:12:26,743
Since when do you know
about horses?

245
00:12:26,910 --> 00:12:27,953
I'm not one to brag.

246
00:12:28,495 --> 00:12:29,996
How'd you do it?
Analyze the form?

247
00:12:30,205 --> 00:12:31,706
Ah, I just picked
the coolest names.

248
00:12:31,915 --> 00:12:33,124
Come on.
Tell me how you won.

249
00:12:34,084 --> 00:12:36,795
- Think about it.
- I hate it when you say that.

250
00:12:45,718 --> 00:12:46,761
How'd they do it?

251
00:12:48,054 --> 00:12:49,097
Kill him?

252
00:12:49,389 --> 00:12:50,890
Baseball bat to the head
most likely.

253
00:12:52,558 --> 00:12:53,601
Oh, God.

254
00:12:54,602 --> 00:12:56,854
Any names spring to mind?
Enemies he may have had?

255
00:12:57,772 --> 00:12:59,148
We're trying to look
into Bill's finances

256
00:12:59,274 --> 00:13:01,651
but we can't find any credit cards
not even a bank account.

257
00:13:02,026 --> 00:13:06,531
No, Bill was funny that way.
He just... didn't trust banks.

258
00:13:07,323 --> 00:13:10,034
Cash only.
Had a safe in his closet.

259
00:13:10,618 --> 00:13:11,661
How long had you known him?

260
00:13:12,912 --> 00:13:14,497
November 6th would've been
4 years.

261
00:13:14,664 --> 00:13:16,499
Was that before or after
he had left horse racing?

262
00:13:18,084 --> 00:13:20,712
Bill didn't leave horse racing.
They suspended him two years ago.

263
00:13:23,256 --> 00:13:26,634
There was a-a pile-up
going into a turn.

264
00:13:28,136 --> 00:13:31,389
They said it was Bill's fault
which it wasn't.

265
00:13:32,765 --> 00:13:33,933
They banned him for a year.

266
00:13:34,517 --> 00:13:35,685
That must have been hard on him.

267
00:13:38,896 --> 00:13:40,732
It was a real dark time.

268
00:13:41,649 --> 00:13:43,860
You know, all Bill ever wanted
to do was ride.

269
00:13:46,195 --> 00:13:48,197
He struggled with his temper.
That's a fact.

270
00:13:50,658 --> 00:13:51,826
Is that why you broke up
with him?

271
00:13:57,999 --> 00:13:59,042
The, uh...

272
00:13:59,792 --> 00:14:01,586
the day he got that job
with Holwell?

273
00:14:03,254 --> 00:14:05,173
We thought we should go out
and celebrate, you know?

274
00:14:06,424 --> 00:14:07,467
Sushi.

275
00:14:08,051 --> 00:14:09,677
Except we got in a fender bender
on the way

276
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:13,181
and uh..
the other driver he...

277
00:14:13,639 --> 00:14:16,184
he's getting all macho
trying to intimidate Bill.

278
00:14:16,809 --> 00:14:19,145
And Bill just went at him
like a crazy person.

279
00:14:19,687 --> 00:14:22,857
You know, he really hurt the guy.

280
00:14:23,608 --> 00:14:24,650
Broke bones.

281
00:14:26,944 --> 00:14:29,238
And when I tried to stop him
he got mad at me.

282
00:14:30,031 --> 00:14:32,283
And we went home
fought half the night

283
00:14:34,869 --> 00:14:36,204
"and I left the next day."

284
00:14:37,830 --> 00:14:39,874
I'm from an abusive family
so, uh...

285
00:14:42,418 --> 00:14:44,295
I see that coming
and I'm out the door.

286
00:14:44,754 --> 00:14:46,589
You catch the guy's name...
the guy he beat up?

287
00:14:47,882 --> 00:14:48,925
No.

288
00:14:49,050 --> 00:14:50,551
Did you see what kinda car
he was driving?

289
00:14:51,177 --> 00:14:52,595
I don't know. Uh...

290
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:57,850
Some kinda gold muscle car.

291
00:14:58,768 --> 00:14:59,936
Black stripes, maybe.

292
00:15:00,978 --> 00:15:02,313
When was the last time
you saw Bill?

293
00:15:03,689 --> 00:15:05,733
I never really saw him again
after I left.

294
00:15:07,985 --> 00:15:10,071
He tried to talk to me
but I didn't want to.

295
00:15:10,863 --> 00:15:13,449
When he died, he had a note
for you in his pocket.

296
00:15:14,784 --> 00:15:15,827
A note?

297
00:15:22,834 --> 00:15:23,876
And this.

298
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:33,803
I shoulda stayed.

299
00:15:36,681 --> 00:15:38,683
I shoulda tried to h-help him.

300
00:15:40,017 --> 00:15:41,644
You do what's right for you, okay?

301
00:15:54,115 --> 00:15:55,825
Guy gets beaten up that bad
maybe he holds a grudge

302
00:15:55,950 --> 00:15:57,368
decides to go back
for round two.

303
00:15:57,493 --> 00:15:59,787
Guy gets beaten that badly
he goes to the ER.

304
00:15:59,996 --> 00:16:01,038
Check admissions
from that night.

305
00:16:01,164 --> 00:16:03,541
Also cross-check DMV records
for gold muscle cars.

306
00:16:03,666 --> 00:16:04,750
Yeah, you got it.

307
00:16:05,084 --> 00:16:07,920
I checked Sutton's apartment.
That safe in the closet's empty.

308
00:16:08,212 --> 00:16:09,255
No money anywhere.

309
00:16:09,755 --> 00:16:12,300
- Almost 20 grand missing.
- 20 grand is motive.

310
00:16:13,176 --> 00:16:14,760
Holwell's running Castor's Folly

311
00:16:14,927 --> 00:16:17,305
in the Montague Pineapple Juice Stakes
this Sunday.

312
00:16:17,972 --> 00:16:19,182
What does that have to do
with anything?

313
00:16:19,307 --> 00:16:22,518
Well, it's a big race.
Big step up for horse and rider.

314
00:16:22,727 --> 00:16:24,437
Rider being Sam Starks.

315
00:16:24,604 --> 00:16:27,356
The apprentice. You think getting
to ride could be motive?

316
00:16:27,982 --> 00:16:29,025
Let's ask her.

317
00:16:29,567 --> 00:16:31,694
Are you sure you just don't wanna
go to play the ponies?

318
00:16:31,944 --> 00:16:34,530
- No playing. Strictly business.
- Sheepdip.

319
00:16:34,906 --> 00:16:36,574
I grew up around horses.
I could come with if you...

320
00:16:36,699 --> 00:16:38,075
Grace, could you check
into that incident

321
00:16:38,242 --> 00:16:39,869
where Sutton got suspended
two years ago?

322
00:16:40,495 --> 00:16:41,537
Thank you.

323
00:16:45,875 --> 00:16:48,294
- Get the hell off my property.
- Whoa, whoa!

324
00:16:48,461 --> 00:16:49,587
What are you doing here anyway?

325
00:16:49,837 --> 00:16:51,797
Easy, Cobb, old buddy.

326
00:16:52,089 --> 00:16:53,132
Is there a problem here?

327
00:16:53,257 --> 00:16:55,760
Yeah, I caught Lockhardt here
sneaking around my stable, spying.

328
00:16:55,885 --> 00:16:57,970
Spying? On your horses?

329
00:16:58,346 --> 00:17:01,349
Like I'd learn something.
I was just being neighborly.

330
00:17:03,392 --> 00:17:06,103
Frank Lockhardt
owner of Ad Astra Stables.

331
00:17:08,064 --> 00:17:10,149
Say, aren't you that cop
that knows about horses?

332
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:12,068
- Jane.
- Jane.

333
00:17:13,027 --> 00:17:15,321
Yeah, I've been hearing about
that trick all day. Very impressive.

334
00:17:15,530 --> 00:17:17,198
Trick? It's no trick.

335
00:17:17,865 --> 00:17:19,325
I actually listen to the animals.

336
00:17:19,825 --> 00:17:21,285
They're very expressive beasts.

337
00:17:23,955 --> 00:17:24,997
Did you hear that?

338
00:17:25,748 --> 00:17:26,791
Doesn't like your suit.

339
00:17:29,252 --> 00:17:32,380
Well, however you did it
congratulations on your choices.

340
00:17:32,797 --> 00:17:35,675
- Two of them were my horses.
- It only takes one horse, Lockhardt.

341
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,511
- You'll see that on Sunday.
- Really? That donkey?

342
00:17:39,011 --> 00:17:40,429
With a little girl in the saddle?

343
00:17:41,055 --> 00:17:42,682
You sure know
how to pick 'em, Cobb.

344
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:44,433
Sutton wasn't any good either.

345
00:17:44,559 --> 00:17:46,644
The only person who'd hire him
was Holwell here.

346
00:17:46,852 --> 00:17:49,146
- Take a hike, Frank.
- No disrespect, Cobb.

347
00:17:49,313 --> 00:17:51,482
We need people like you
in the horse business.

348
00:17:51,649 --> 00:17:53,568
I mean, without fools and dreamers
where would we be?

349
00:17:54,443 --> 00:17:55,945
Can't have winners
without losers, right?

350
00:17:56,070 --> 00:17:58,781
Castor's Folly is gonna win
on Sunday. You'll see.

351
00:17:58,906 --> 00:18:00,950
Pride and love of these animals
beats your money

352
00:18:01,075 --> 00:18:02,577
and corporate charts
any day of the week.

353
00:18:02,702 --> 00:18:04,203
- Come on.
- That's enough, gentlemen.

354
00:18:05,079 --> 00:18:07,039
We need to speak with Sam Starks.
Do you know where she is?

355
00:18:07,164 --> 00:18:08,207
We need to speak with her.

356
00:18:18,718 --> 00:18:19,760
Watch it! He'll kick.

357
00:18:22,430 --> 00:18:25,641
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

358
00:18:25,808 --> 00:18:27,768
Sorry, Mr. Holwell.
I don't know what happens.

359
00:18:28,269 --> 00:18:30,563
It's not your fault.
He's just not ready.

360
00:18:35,276 --> 00:18:36,611
Is that Castor's Folly?

361
00:18:37,445 --> 00:18:38,738
No, it's Pollock's Dream.

362
00:18:40,281 --> 00:18:41,324
It's his twin.

363
00:18:42,491 --> 00:18:43,701
His evil twin.

364
00:18:44,702 --> 00:18:47,830
But we'll fix him, eventually.
Right, Sam?

365
00:18:49,415 --> 00:18:50,458
Yes, Mr. Holwell.

366
00:18:50,583 --> 00:18:53,336
Ms. Starks, I'd like to ask you
some more questions.

367
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:55,588
Um, I don't know if...

368
00:18:55,796 --> 00:18:58,382
No, go ahead, Sam.
Talk to the lady. I got this.

369
00:19:04,889 --> 00:19:05,931
Twins.

370
00:19:07,183 --> 00:19:10,061
- That's rare, huh?
- Yep.

371
00:19:11,145 --> 00:19:12,563
Temperaments are completely different

372
00:19:12,688 --> 00:19:15,816
but each like their dam
in their own way.

373
00:19:17,276 --> 00:19:19,362
Someday they'll both be winners
like she was.

374
00:19:20,071 --> 00:19:22,365
If this bastard will ever let
a rider on him, that is.

375
00:19:22,531 --> 00:19:24,408
So Frank Lockhardt's wrong
about your horses.

376
00:19:24,784 --> 00:19:27,078
Well, the great thing
about racing is, uh...

377
00:19:27,536 --> 00:19:28,913
the more
they underestimate you

378
00:19:29,038 --> 00:19:30,873
the better the odds are
when you win.

379
00:19:31,374 --> 00:19:32,458
The more money you make.

380
00:19:33,167 --> 00:19:34,335
And win we will.

381
00:19:35,002 --> 00:19:36,045
Mark my words.

382
00:19:36,671 --> 00:19:38,047
It's gotta be expensive though...

383
00:19:38,422 --> 00:19:41,008
the upkeep on a horse
that won't let himself be ridden.

384
00:19:41,217 --> 00:19:43,636
Well, people say I'm an old fool
for keeping Poll around

385
00:19:43,761 --> 00:19:44,929
but screw 'em.

386
00:19:45,262 --> 00:19:47,473
The boys are like mirror images
of each other.

387
00:19:47,723 --> 00:19:50,017
The flaws of one
are the strengths of the other.

388
00:19:50,643 --> 00:19:52,520
Keep 'em together
and they'll rub off on each other.

389
00:19:52,687 --> 00:19:53,729
I've seen it happen.

390
00:19:54,146 --> 00:19:55,606
So this one...

391
00:19:59,527 --> 00:20:01,195
Keeps this one
from going crazy.

392
00:20:02,196 --> 00:20:03,656
And what does this one
bring to the mix?

393
00:20:04,615 --> 00:20:07,326
- Oh, he runs like the north wind.
- Ah.

394
00:20:12,164 --> 00:20:13,207
Hello there.

395
00:20:19,296 --> 00:20:20,339
Uh-huh.

396
00:20:20,881 --> 00:20:21,924
Mr. Jane?

397
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,343
Uh-huh.

398
00:20:25,386 --> 00:20:26,429
Okay.

399
00:20:30,516 --> 00:20:31,559
Really?

400
00:20:33,310 --> 00:20:35,229
Oh. Oh. Excuse me.

401
00:20:35,855 --> 00:20:38,691
We'll talk again soon.
Okay.

402
00:20:39,942 --> 00:20:41,068
Grace. What's up?

403
00:20:41,694 --> 00:20:43,779
I got the scoop
on that pile-up Sutton caused.

404
00:20:44,155 --> 00:20:46,615
Three jockeys were injured...
one of 'em pretty badly.

405
00:20:47,116 --> 00:20:48,409
Ah, that'd be Barnes.

406
00:20:49,076 --> 00:20:51,162
Yeah. He had
multiple broken bones

407
00:20:51,328 --> 00:20:52,663
and spent almost a month
in the hospital.

408
00:20:52,955 --> 00:20:53,998
Ouch.

409
00:20:59,378 --> 00:21:01,922
With Sutton dead, you're getting
a big break as a jockey.

410
00:21:02,381 --> 00:21:03,758
Must be pretty exciting, huh?

411
00:21:04,508 --> 00:21:06,302
I guess. Sure.

412
00:21:06,969 --> 00:21:09,722
Come on. You had to have known
with Sutton gone

413
00:21:09,847 --> 00:21:11,432
that Holwell would probably
go to you.

414
00:21:13,809 --> 00:21:14,852
You don't understand.

415
00:21:15,227 --> 00:21:17,813
Bill was the closest thing
to a family I've ever had.

416
00:21:18,314 --> 00:21:20,316
I'd give anything
to get him back.

417
00:21:20,858 --> 00:21:23,694
But I can't.
Riding's all I have.

418
00:21:24,278 --> 00:21:25,321
It's all I know.

419
00:21:25,446 --> 00:21:26,781
Must be a lot of pressure
on you.

420
00:21:27,656 --> 00:21:28,699
I can handle it.

421
00:21:29,158 --> 00:21:30,367
Then what are you so afraid of?

422
00:21:31,494 --> 00:21:34,121
- I'm not afraid.
- Mm... are too.

423
00:21:35,331 --> 00:21:37,792
Is somebody threatening you?
We can help.

424
00:21:39,418 --> 00:21:41,295
I'm fine. I don't need help.

425
00:21:42,421 --> 00:21:44,048
Are we done?
Can I go?

426
00:21:44,882 --> 00:21:45,925
Sure.

427
00:21:49,845 --> 00:21:51,722
Tough girl. Scared, though.

428
00:21:52,848 --> 00:21:54,767
-Terrified, even.
- Of what?

429
00:21:55,434 --> 00:21:58,479
Ah, there's the rub.
Of what is she so scared?

430
00:21:58,604 --> 00:21:59,980
And the answer is...

431
00:22:00,105 --> 00:22:02,900
Well, it's a rhetorical question.
I have no idea.

432
00:22:03,150 --> 00:22:04,693
Well, I do have an idea
but I'm not gonna tell you

433
00:22:04,819 --> 00:22:06,153
because that
would be premature.

434
00:22:06,612 --> 00:22:09,990
And I am not gonna amuse you
by demanding to know, so there.

435
00:22:10,950 --> 00:22:12,076
So we're both happy then.

436
00:22:16,413 --> 00:22:18,123
So this could be the guy
that Sutton beat up.

437
00:22:18,290 --> 00:22:20,751
Philip Debolt came through ER
with a broken jaw

438
00:22:20,876 --> 00:22:22,586
and contusions
wouldn't say what happened.

439
00:22:22,878 --> 00:22:24,421
He's got a couple
of disorderly conducts.

440
00:22:24,672 --> 00:22:26,131
Gold muscle car
with black stripes.

441
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:28,217
Symbol of bullying jerks
the world over.

442
00:22:28,384 --> 00:22:29,426
Nice new rims.

443
00:22:30,636 --> 00:22:33,264
Mechanic's gone for the day.
Open tomorrow at 8:00.

444
00:22:33,722 --> 00:22:35,641
Nice chrome rims
on that Mustang out there.

445
00:22:36,308 --> 00:22:39,061
- You're, uh, Phil, I'm guessing.
- Yep.

446
00:22:39,728 --> 00:22:41,105
Expensive, those rims.

447
00:22:42,314 --> 00:22:43,941
And that bling you got there
must have set you back.

448
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:50,322
There a problem?

449
00:22:51,365 --> 00:22:52,408
Yeah. Here's the problem.

450
00:22:52,825 --> 00:22:54,326
Man's dead
and 20 grand is missing.

451
00:22:54,743 --> 00:22:55,953
Looks like you and your car
are wearing it.

452
00:22:56,537 --> 00:22:58,455
- Who's dead?
- Well, take a wild guess.

453
00:23:01,208 --> 00:23:02,918
Wait, not... not Bill Sutton.

454
00:23:05,504 --> 00:23:06,547
- He's dead?
- Yeah.

455
00:23:06,964 --> 00:23:09,466
That's what happens when you hit
someone that hard, Phil.

456
00:23:10,301 --> 00:23:12,428
I didn't hit him.
He hit me.

457
00:23:12,553 --> 00:23:13,888
And he broke your jaw
humiliated you

458
00:23:14,013 --> 00:23:15,055
so you went after him
got your revenge.

459
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:18,100
No, it wasn't like that. I mean
yeah, when I saw the guy

460
00:23:18,225 --> 00:23:19,560
I wanted to beat the hell
out of him, sure.

461
00:23:19,685 --> 00:23:21,645
- You talked to him. When?
- He came to the hospital.

462
00:23:22,354 --> 00:23:24,773
- His girlfriend had left him.
- Wait. He visited you at the hospital?

463
00:23:25,399 --> 00:23:26,525
To get things right with me.

464
00:23:27,318 --> 00:23:28,360
To make amends.

465
00:23:29,194 --> 00:23:30,905
I mean, everything in his life
was screwed up

466
00:23:31,822 --> 00:23:32,907
but he wanted to fix it.

467
00:23:34,491 --> 00:23:35,951
Gave me $18,000.

468
00:23:36,911 --> 00:23:39,038
Said he was gonna live his life
straight from then on.

469
00:23:41,457 --> 00:23:42,708
Hey, look, guys, uh...

470
00:23:43,125 --> 00:23:44,501
don't tell the guys
I got beat up.

471
00:23:45,586 --> 00:23:47,171
Kinda said it was a car accident.

472
00:23:49,548 --> 00:23:50,591
Thanks for your time.

473
00:24:10,736 --> 00:24:12,988
- Workin' late?
- Um, just finishing up.

474
00:24:14,156 --> 00:24:15,783
- Stay a while. Chat.
- Let go of me.

475
00:24:15,908 --> 00:24:17,242
Nobody rides for Holwell, see?

476
00:24:17,701 --> 00:24:19,536
- You ride for him, you don't ride again.
- Let go.

477
00:24:19,662 --> 00:24:22,331
Most riders are smart enough to listen.
Don't be one of the stupid ones.

478
00:24:22,456 --> 00:24:23,499
You don't understand.
I don't have a choice...

479
00:24:23,624 --> 00:24:26,418
Look what happened to Sutton.
You want that to happen to you?

480
00:24:26,710 --> 00:24:27,795
"Let her be, Barnes."

481
00:24:31,757 --> 00:24:34,218
Oh, you're a nasty piece
of work, aren't you?

482
00:24:35,135 --> 00:24:37,680
Ah? I knew that from the moment
I saw you

483
00:24:37,846 --> 00:24:40,391
but I didn't think you'd stoop so low
to threaten young girls.

484
00:24:41,850 --> 00:24:43,185
- I've had enough of you.
- Hang on.

485
00:24:43,310 --> 00:24:44,561
No, no.
Whoa, whoa, that's not fair.

486
00:24:45,646 --> 00:24:47,731
Stop! Drop the weapon.

487
00:24:47,856 --> 00:24:49,733
Put your hands in the air
where I can see 'em!

488
00:24:53,696 --> 00:24:54,738
Huh?

489
00:24:58,867 --> 00:25:00,577
And good thing for you
you're a terrible liar.

490
00:25:00,703 --> 00:25:02,121
It's all about the eye contact.

491
00:25:07,668 --> 00:25:09,086
That close. Huh?

492
00:25:11,422 --> 00:25:12,464
Stop it.

493
00:25:17,511 --> 00:25:18,929
Really? Put it down.

494
00:25:27,769 --> 00:25:28,895
Ellis Barnes has a temper.

495
00:25:29,062 --> 00:25:31,273
Popped twice for assault
got probation. Tough guy.

496
00:25:31,732 --> 00:25:33,817
Hold up.
I've got an idea.

497
00:25:34,818 --> 00:25:36,194
"You don't understand.
I don't have a choice."

498
00:25:36,319 --> 00:25:37,654
"Look what happened to Sutton."

499
00:25:38,447 --> 00:25:39,740
"You want that to happen to you?"

500
00:25:41,450 --> 00:25:43,285
Bill Sutton had his head
bashed in.

501
00:25:43,952 --> 00:25:44,995
Did you have something
to do with that?

502
00:25:45,120 --> 00:25:46,163
This is all a misunderstanding.

503
00:25:46,288 --> 00:25:47,706
I was just saying
Starks should be careful.

504
00:25:48,081 --> 00:25:49,124
Friendly advice.

505
00:25:49,541 --> 00:25:51,835
Friendly advice not to ride
for Cobb Holwell.

506
00:25:52,878 --> 00:25:54,171
Why would you care
about that?

507
00:25:54,838 --> 00:25:57,632
I have many interests...
some large, some small.

508
00:25:57,841 --> 00:26:00,093
One of which is hating
Bill Sutton.

509
00:26:01,428 --> 00:26:03,805
We know he put you under
at that race, Mr. Barnes.

510
00:26:03,930 --> 00:26:06,183
- Ended your career.
- He did it on purpose.

511
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:07,642
I know he did.

512
00:26:08,477 --> 00:26:10,437
Somebody did that to me
you know what I'd do?

513
00:26:11,313 --> 00:26:12,397
I'd kill him.

514
00:26:14,024 --> 00:26:15,067
Well, that's you.

515
00:26:17,027 --> 00:26:18,653
So is there anything else
or are we done here?

516
00:26:19,362 --> 00:26:20,405
Just one more thing.

517
00:26:25,952 --> 00:26:26,995
Mr. Barnes...

518
00:26:28,288 --> 00:26:29,664
I'm from the California Racing Board.

519
00:26:30,624 --> 00:26:32,626
We contacted the CRB
when we brought you in.

520
00:26:32,751 --> 00:26:34,211
- It's routine.
- I don't understand.

521
00:26:34,336 --> 00:26:36,213
You've been selling inside information
to bettors, Mr. Barnes.

522
00:26:36,338 --> 00:26:37,798
Either that information is genuine

523
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:39,633
which is a heinous breach
of your contract

524
00:26:39,841 --> 00:26:42,511
or it is false, and you are
simply defrauding people.

525
00:26:42,719 --> 00:26:45,347
Either way
pending a full investigation

526
00:26:45,514 --> 00:26:48,266
- I am obliged to ban you from all state...
- Wait, no, I'm a groom.

527
00:26:48,391 --> 00:26:50,143
- How am I supposed to earn?
- However.

528
00:26:51,353 --> 00:26:54,606
Agent Lisbon has asked me
to exercise some discretion here

529
00:26:55,774 --> 00:26:57,859
based on your willingness
to assist her in this...

530
00:26:58,443 --> 00:26:59,486
murder investigation.

531
00:27:05,742 --> 00:27:06,785
All righty then.

532
00:27:08,870 --> 00:27:09,913
Wait.

533
00:27:16,044 --> 00:27:17,212
I didn't kill Sutton.

534
00:27:17,796 --> 00:27:19,714
All I did is threaten him
and threaten Starks.

535
00:27:19,923 --> 00:27:21,550
Who asked you to do that
Mr. Barnes?

536
00:27:21,716 --> 00:27:23,009
Talking to people is no crime.

537
00:27:23,552 --> 00:27:24,594
Who?

538
00:27:26,972 --> 00:27:30,142
Frank Lockhardt
owner of the Ad Astra Stable.

539
00:27:34,271 --> 00:27:35,313
Grace, where is everybody?

540
00:27:35,689 --> 00:27:37,983
Oh. Somewhere else
doing interesting things.

541
00:27:38,108 --> 00:27:39,151
Okay. Come on. Let's go.

542
00:27:40,277 --> 00:27:41,319
- Go where?
- Come on.

543
00:27:41,778 --> 00:27:43,738
- Wait. Did you okay this with Lisbon?
- I certainly did.

544
00:27:44,072 --> 00:27:45,407
What kinda question
is that, anyway?

545
00:27:45,532 --> 00:27:46,783
It's almost like you don't trust me.

546
00:27:47,117 --> 00:27:49,786
We have to stop by your place
on the way, get a different outfit.

547
00:27:50,120 --> 00:27:51,788
- An outfit for what?
- Uh...

548
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:58,712
Sam Starks, Grace Van Pelt.

549
00:27:59,087 --> 00:28:00,881
- Grace, this is Sam Starks.
- Hi.

550
00:28:01,006 --> 00:28:02,048
Hello.

551
00:28:03,300 --> 00:28:05,218
Grace used to ride.
She grew up around horses.

552
00:28:05,427 --> 00:28:07,429
Dressage, mostly.
A little jumping.

553
00:28:07,679 --> 00:28:08,930
So let's get her a ride, huh?

554
00:28:09,347 --> 00:28:11,349
- Um... a ride?
- Yeah.

555
00:28:12,350 --> 00:28:14,728
- Um... I don't know.
- Sam...

556
00:28:16,605 --> 00:28:18,565
We're cops.
We're police officers.

557
00:28:21,443 --> 00:28:22,485
Okay.

558
00:28:22,611 --> 00:28:24,613
- There we go. Thank you.
- I guess.

559
00:28:25,739 --> 00:28:27,866
Now we're talking. Have fun.

560
00:28:29,159 --> 00:28:31,328
- Hi.
- This is Castor's Folly.

561
00:28:32,495 --> 00:28:33,538
Be safe.

562
00:28:35,790 --> 00:28:37,292
Look, I'm a businessman.

563
00:28:37,542 --> 00:28:39,377
Horses are nothing
but a hobby for me.

564
00:28:40,170 --> 00:28:41,213
Right.

565
00:28:41,588 --> 00:28:43,757
- You're a developer.
- Commercial, mostly.

566
00:28:45,592 --> 00:28:47,510
You wanna get your hands
on Cobb Holwell's stable.

567
00:28:47,886 --> 00:28:49,304
I wanna beat him, sure.

568
00:28:49,638 --> 00:28:51,848
I like winning races
as much as the next man.

569
00:28:52,057 --> 00:28:53,391
Not your hobby.
Your business.

570
00:28:54,309 --> 00:28:56,144
You wanna develop
the Redwood Downs complex.

571
00:28:56,811 --> 00:28:58,688
Holwell has his own stable there
and he won't sell to you.

572
00:28:58,855 --> 00:29:01,233
Well, there was some discussion
about developing Redwood Downs

573
00:29:01,358 --> 00:29:04,110
but nothing concrete.
It's just talk.

574
00:29:04,402 --> 00:29:05,987
Talk that could lead
to millions in revenues.

575
00:29:06,404 --> 00:29:07,739
But first you'd need Holwell's stable.

576
00:29:08,657 --> 00:29:09,699
So?

577
00:29:09,824 --> 00:29:10,867
So you'd like seeing Holwell
outta business.

578
00:29:11,159 --> 00:29:13,411
That's why you paid Ellis Barnes
to stop jockeys riding for him.

579
00:29:16,122 --> 00:29:18,667
Let's say Barnes told jockeys
that if they ride for Holwell

580
00:29:18,792 --> 00:29:20,293
that means they won't ride
for me.

581
00:29:20,502 --> 00:29:22,087
So what? It's the truth.

582
00:29:22,587 --> 00:29:23,797
No law's been broken.

583
00:29:27,592 --> 00:29:29,594
Bill Sutton was responsible
for the accident

584
00:29:29,761 --> 00:29:31,179
that crippled Barnes.
Did you know that?

585
00:29:33,014 --> 00:29:35,100
Barnes was angry about it.
Very angry.

586
00:29:37,435 --> 00:29:40,021
Now you sent a very angry man to threaten
the person he was angry with.

587
00:29:40,438 --> 00:29:41,648
How'd you think
that would turn out?

588
00:29:49,406 --> 00:29:50,865
I think I want my attorney.

589
00:30:01,751 --> 00:30:02,794
That was fun.

590
00:30:05,463 --> 00:30:06,506
What horse is that?

591
00:30:06,673 --> 00:30:08,008
Well, too bad you're so tall

592
00:30:08,133 --> 00:30:09,759
'cause Holwell could use
a second jockey

593
00:30:09,884 --> 00:30:11,970
for Pollock's Dream here.
He's ready to be ridden.

594
00:30:12,429 --> 00:30:13,555
I thought he was the crazy one.

595
00:30:13,888 --> 00:30:15,598
Oh, no, no, he's just...

596
00:30:16,224 --> 00:30:17,809
He's just a little misunderstood.

597
00:30:18,184 --> 00:30:20,145
- He seems like a sweetie.
- Isn't he?

598
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:21,563
Why don't you hop on?

599
00:30:22,939 --> 00:30:23,982
Oh, I don't know.

600
00:30:24,107 --> 00:30:26,943
Oh, I know horses
and he is 100% safe.

601
00:30:27,152 --> 00:30:29,112
- Look at that. See?
- Yeah?

602
00:30:29,446 --> 00:30:30,739
He's nodding. Jump on.

603
00:30:32,365 --> 00:30:33,742
Oh, I don't know.

604
00:30:34,284 --> 00:30:35,994
- Come on.
- Okay.

605
00:30:38,246 --> 00:30:39,789
Ready and lift.

606
00:30:44,419 --> 00:30:45,462
Okay.

607
00:30:46,755 --> 00:30:48,256
Huh? See? Look at that.

608
00:30:49,132 --> 00:30:50,175
What did I say?

609
00:30:50,884 --> 00:30:52,719
Hey! Get off that horse!

610
00:30:55,055 --> 00:30:57,724
- Are you trying to get yourself killed?
- I'm sorry, Sam. I didn't know.

611
00:31:00,685 --> 00:31:01,936
Relax, Sam.

612
00:31:02,604 --> 00:31:03,688
Poll was telling me he was ready.

613
00:31:03,813 --> 00:31:06,232
I was just proving that Holwell
was right to believe in his horse.

614
00:31:06,358 --> 00:31:07,567
There's no need to thank me.

615
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:09,402
Thank you?

616
00:31:09,611 --> 00:31:11,780
You trying to get me fired
the day before my big race?

617
00:31:11,946 --> 00:31:13,823
- Yeah. Thanks.
- Sam, I'm sorry...

618
00:31:13,948 --> 00:31:16,368
Mr. Holwell is gonna be so mad
when he hears.

619
00:31:16,576 --> 00:31:18,828
- Please... you have to leave now.
- Okay.

620
00:31:20,497 --> 00:31:21,539
See you, pal.

621
00:31:22,540 --> 00:31:23,666
See you, Pollock's Dream.

622
00:31:24,959 --> 00:31:26,628
- Bye.
- What was that all about?

623
00:31:27,212 --> 00:31:29,214
Clarity, Grace. Clarity.

624
00:31:31,508 --> 00:31:33,259
- Hello, Lisbon.
- Where have you been?

625
00:31:33,551 --> 00:31:35,053
Oh, horseback riding
with Grace.

626
00:31:35,178 --> 00:31:38,598
Oh, that's nice. We've been trying to get
confessions outta Lockhardt and Barnes.

627
00:31:38,807 --> 00:31:40,850
- And how's that going for you?
- "It's not."

628
00:31:41,101 --> 00:31:43,645
Oh, well, surprise.
You can set him free.

629
00:31:43,978 --> 00:31:45,021
Because?

630
00:31:45,146 --> 00:31:48,066
Because I come bearing
a practical and speedy solution

631
00:31:48,191 --> 00:31:50,235
for all your crime detection problems.

632
00:31:50,443 --> 00:31:52,570
- Really?
- Really and truly.

633
00:31:52,862 --> 00:31:54,364
We are off to the races.

634
00:31:59,786 --> 00:32:00,829
Hey!

635
00:32:08,484 --> 00:32:11,279
"Final results from our race
in fifth division"

636
00:32:11,404 --> 00:32:15,616
"but first, Eddie Moon in second,
coming in third was Kindly Dilemma"

637
00:32:16,117 --> 00:32:18,870
"followed by Gift for Mary
and Fortune's Favor."

638
00:32:21,080 --> 00:32:24,709
"Horses for our final race
are now in the paddock area."

639
00:32:28,713 --> 00:32:29,756
Everybody in position?

640
00:32:30,757 --> 00:32:31,799
I'm here.

641
00:32:33,634 --> 00:32:35,470
- "Van Pelt?"
- Here.

642
00:32:36,929 --> 00:32:37,972
"Cho?"

643
00:32:38,389 --> 00:32:40,558
- Here.
- Anybody got eyes on Jane?

644
00:32:46,397 --> 00:32:47,482
Come on, people.

645
00:32:54,364 --> 00:32:55,865
"Your attention, please."

646
00:32:56,032 --> 00:33:00,119
"The horses are beginning to file onto
the track for the final race of the day."

647
00:33:00,453 --> 00:33:05,500
"The $200,000 Montague Pineapple
Juice Stakes at six and a half furlongs."

648
00:33:05,625 --> 00:33:06,667
Wait a minute. I got him.

649
00:33:08,127 --> 00:33:09,796
- Oh, hey.
- Hey.

650
00:33:12,340 --> 00:33:14,092
This is the guy.
One, two, three.

651
00:33:14,509 --> 00:33:16,511
- This guy knows his horses.
- "Next."

652
00:33:19,305 --> 00:33:20,348
Next.

653
00:33:21,265 --> 00:33:23,935
- Hmm. After you.
- Oh, okay.

654
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:27,438
10 large on Castor's Folly to win.

655
00:33:27,814 --> 00:33:29,565
Castor's Folly, $10,000.

656
00:33:31,150 --> 00:33:33,694
Castor's Folly.
100 to 1.

657
00:33:36,322 --> 00:33:37,365
Next.

658
00:33:37,865 --> 00:33:38,908
Castor's Folly.

659
00:33:51,212 --> 00:33:53,256
Now don't let him have his head
in the early turns.

660
00:33:53,423 --> 00:33:55,216
He'll wanna get out fast
but don't let him.

661
00:33:55,633 --> 00:33:56,676
Okay.

662
00:33:57,093 --> 00:33:59,595
I know you're behind
that police harassment, Holwell.

663
00:34:00,304 --> 00:34:01,848
You might've had your fun
yesterday

664
00:34:02,098 --> 00:34:03,766
but I'm gonna own
your stable tomorrow.

665
00:34:05,435 --> 00:34:07,103
Well, that's unless he wins today.

666
00:34:07,645 --> 00:34:08,688
What?

667
00:34:08,813 --> 00:34:10,148
Well, if he wins today
then, uh...

668
00:34:10,356 --> 00:34:12,066
he makes enough money
to pay off all his debts.

669
00:34:12,233 --> 00:34:14,402
He's got exactly zero chance
of winning.

670
00:34:14,569 --> 00:34:16,612
- It's 100 to 1.
- I know, great odds, isn't it?

671
00:34:16,821 --> 00:34:19,699
- I got $10,000 on him to win.
- What?

672
00:34:20,241 --> 00:34:22,326
You're a fool. But hey...

673
00:34:23,494 --> 00:34:25,079
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

674
00:34:28,124 --> 00:34:29,584
Did you really bet
on Castor's Folly?

675
00:34:30,001 --> 00:34:31,043
Of course I did.

676
00:34:31,294 --> 00:34:33,504
I mean, he's gonna win, isn't he?
What's wrong?

677
00:34:34,088 --> 00:34:35,965
A bet that big
will shorten the odds.

678
00:34:36,132 --> 00:34:37,216
I'll win less money.

679
00:34:37,758 --> 00:34:38,801
What did you bet?

680
00:34:38,926 --> 00:34:41,304
- Every penny I have.
- Well, that's confident.

681
00:34:42,346 --> 00:34:43,389
Desperate.

682
00:34:43,514 --> 00:34:46,350
"And the horses are all going
into the gate..."

683
00:34:49,228 --> 00:34:51,606
Well... not to worry.

684
00:34:51,939 --> 00:34:53,065
He's a cinch.

685
00:34:53,858 --> 00:34:54,984
I can guarantee it.

686
00:34:55,985 --> 00:34:57,069
- Is that right?
- Mm-Hmm.

687
00:34:57,195 --> 00:34:59,697
- How's that?
- A little switcheroo of the horsies.

688
00:35:00,323 --> 00:35:03,159
- What do you mean?
- Castor's Folly and Pollock's Dream...

689
00:35:03,576 --> 00:35:05,203
I switched them in their stalls.

690
00:35:06,204 --> 00:35:09,165
- Don't joke. It's not funny.
- I know you don't think Polly's ready

691
00:35:09,290 --> 00:35:11,167
but I'm telling you, he is
and I know horses.

692
00:35:11,292 --> 00:35:14,504
And you said yourself,
Pollock's Dream is the faster horse.

693
00:35:15,087 --> 00:35:17,673
- Tell me you're not serious.
- They look exactly alike.

694
00:35:17,798 --> 00:35:19,592
Even if the steward
suspected anything

695
00:35:19,717 --> 00:35:21,135
you would've been so surprised

696
00:35:21,302 --> 00:35:23,513
they would have thought
it was an honest mistake.

697
00:35:23,763 --> 00:35:24,805
But they didn't.

698
00:35:25,389 --> 00:35:27,058
So my plan has worked perfectly.

699
00:35:28,893 --> 00:35:31,312
"And they're off.
It's Musketeer's Cat in the lead"

700
00:35:31,437 --> 00:35:33,773
"Calm Thunder in second
Temper's Twilight in third"

701
00:35:33,898 --> 00:35:36,901
"Papa Gene in fourth.
Sheba's Ghost is slow to get going..."

702
00:35:37,193 --> 00:35:38,653
You meddling ass!

703
00:35:39,237 --> 00:35:42,240
I already switched the horses.
You switched them back!

704
00:35:42,532 --> 00:35:44,242
That's how Sutton
ended up dead, isn't it?

705
00:35:44,575 --> 00:35:47,161
He refused to go along
with your plan so you killed him.

706
00:35:47,787 --> 00:35:50,373
And you coerced that poor girl
into taking his place.

707
00:35:50,915 --> 00:35:52,333
You son of a bitch.

708
00:35:54,377 --> 00:35:55,878
That works as a confession, doesn't it?

709
00:35:57,672 --> 00:35:59,131
"Now it's Musketeer's Cat in first."

710
00:35:59,257 --> 00:36:01,634
"Calm Thunder and Temper's Twilight
in third by the rail."

711
00:36:01,842 --> 00:36:02,885
"Sheba's Ghost going up fourth."

712
00:36:03,010 --> 00:36:04,470
"Neck and neck with Papa Gene
on the outside"

713
00:36:04,720 --> 00:36:06,347
"alongside Castor's Folly."

714
00:36:06,597 --> 00:36:08,057
"Coming into the turn
it's Calm Thunder."

715
00:36:08,224 --> 00:36:09,308
"Musketeer's Cat in the lead."

716
00:36:09,433 --> 00:36:11,143
"Then Temper's Twilight
is falling back in fifth."

717
00:36:11,269 --> 00:36:13,646
"Castor's Folly's on
the outside surging ahead."

718
00:36:13,813 --> 00:36:16,357
"Then Ocean Strider pulling up
to seventh. Lucky Boy trailing."

719
00:36:16,732 --> 00:36:18,818
"Rounding turn number two,
it's Musketeer's Cat in the lead"

720
00:36:18,943 --> 00:36:21,654
"and Calm Thunder in second.
Castor's Folly's coming in fast"

721
00:36:21,862 --> 00:36:23,823
"on the outside running upon
Temper's Twilight."

722
00:36:23,948 --> 00:36:24,991
No!

723
00:36:25,116 --> 00:36:26,158
"They're bunched up coming
into the back stretch."

724
00:36:26,325 --> 00:36:27,785
"It's Musketeer's Cat,
and Castor's Folly"

725
00:36:27,994 --> 00:36:29,537
"passing Calm Thunder
for second place."

726
00:36:29,745 --> 00:36:32,540
"Papa Gene is trying to stay in it.
Sheba's Ghost is holding in fifth."

727
00:36:32,665 --> 00:36:35,001
"Four lengths back, it's
Ocean Strider and Lucky Boy."

728
00:36:35,501 --> 00:36:37,044
"Coming into turn three
it's Musketeer's Cat"

729
00:36:37,169 --> 00:36:40,840
"by a length and a half. Castor's Folly
down the center chasing in second."

730
00:36:41,007 --> 00:36:42,883
"Calm Thunder is holding off
Papa Gene at the rail."

731
00:36:43,092 --> 00:36:44,468
"Sheba's Ghost is still running
in fifth."

732
00:36:44,594 --> 00:36:46,637
"Lucky Boy's making a run
at Ocean Strider."

733
00:36:46,804 --> 00:36:50,057
"In first, Musketeer's Cat's in trouble
as Castor's Folly picks up speed."

734
00:36:50,182 --> 00:36:52,393
"Calm Thunder's trying to stay
in it. Papa Gene's falling back."

735
00:36:52,518 --> 00:36:55,563
"Out of turn four,
it's Musketeer's Cat by a length."

736
00:36:55,730 --> 00:36:57,273
"Castor's Folly, second... Calm Thunder."

737
00:36:57,398 --> 00:36:58,441
"Castor's Folly closing in fast
on Musketeer's Cat"

738
00:36:58,566 --> 00:36:59,650
"as they head
down to the wire."

739
00:36:59,817 --> 00:37:02,194
"Musketeer's Cat by half a length.
Castor's Folly and Calm Thunder."

740
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:03,654
"Musketeer's Cat
then Castor's Folly."

741
00:37:04,071 --> 00:37:06,073
"It's neck and neck.
Musketeer's Cat Springs for the finish."

742
00:37:06,240 --> 00:37:07,533
"Castor's Folly
trying to take the lead."

743
00:37:07,658 --> 00:37:12,121
"Musketeer's Cat switching hard.
Castor's Folly's right there..."

744
00:37:12,246 --> 00:37:13,372
"Pushing ahead is Castor's Folly."

745
00:37:13,497 --> 00:37:15,082
"Castor's Folly takes the lead."

746
00:37:15,374 --> 00:37:17,585
"Castor's Folly wins by a nose."

747
00:37:18,085 --> 00:37:19,712
"Castor's Folly takes
first place."

748
00:37:19,920 --> 00:37:22,673
"Musketeer's Cat in second
Calm Thunder in third"

749
00:37:22,882 --> 00:37:27,094
"and Papa Gene, Sheba's Ghost
Temper's Twilight..."

750
00:37:27,303 --> 00:37:30,640
Mr. Holwell, you're under arrest
for the murder of Bill Sutton.

751
00:37:32,725 --> 00:37:33,976
But you switched the horses.

752
00:37:34,143 --> 00:37:36,729
Uh, I just said that.
I didn't really.

753
00:37:36,896 --> 00:37:38,439
Congratulations.
Your ringer won.

754
00:38:03,756 --> 00:38:04,840
- Murder weapon?
- Yeah.

755
00:38:04,965 --> 00:38:07,176
Lug wrench from Holwell's truck...
Sutton's D.N.A. is all over it.

756
00:38:07,301 --> 00:38:10,054
That and Sam Stark's testimony
will put Holwell away for good.

757
00:38:10,721 --> 00:38:12,223
He told her straight out
that he killed Sutton

758
00:38:12,348 --> 00:38:13,974
to get her to cooperate
with his scheme.

759
00:38:14,684 --> 00:38:17,687
Said that she'd never ride again
or end up dead if she talked.

760
00:38:18,187 --> 00:38:19,730
She was young and naive enough
to believe it.

761
00:38:19,939 --> 00:38:21,065
I still don't get the scheme.

762
00:38:21,232 --> 00:38:22,858
Why didn't Holwell just run
the fast horse?

763
00:38:23,067 --> 00:38:24,485
Well, the odds are no good
on a fast horse.

764
00:38:24,610 --> 00:38:26,320
Everybody bets on him.
It's pennies on the dollar.

765
00:38:26,487 --> 00:38:28,197
Yeah, you run the slow horse
to get the long odds

766
00:38:28,322 --> 00:38:29,949
and then you run the fast horse
to win the money.

767
00:38:30,324 --> 00:38:32,785
But how did he switch the horses?
Don't they check for that?

768
00:38:32,910 --> 00:38:35,162
Well, Holwell gave the fast one
a lip tattoo to match the slow one

769
00:38:35,287 --> 00:38:36,706
so the stewards
couldn't tell them apart.

770
00:38:42,002 --> 00:38:43,045
Ms. Lecure.

771
00:38:45,965 --> 00:38:48,050
I asked evidence
to release this.

772
00:38:48,843 --> 00:38:52,304
Mr. Sutton wanted you to have it
and I think you should.

773
00:38:58,436 --> 00:39:00,104
You know, I think
we would've been okay.

774
00:39:01,897 --> 00:39:04,525
I mean, if we had... time.

775
00:39:08,863 --> 00:39:09,905
I think we would have.

776
00:39:11,824 --> 00:39:12,867
Good luck.

777
00:39:13,993 --> 00:39:15,035
Thanks.

778
00:39:19,457 --> 00:39:21,959
Fool to herself, that girl.
It was never gonna work.

779
00:39:22,334 --> 00:39:23,502
Don't be so cynical.

780
00:39:23,627 --> 00:39:25,629
Oh, you did let Sam Starks go,
didn't you?

781
00:39:26,380 --> 00:39:28,257
She was a mere tool
an innocent pawn.

782
00:39:28,424 --> 00:39:31,427
Semi-innocent, but, yeah
she's free and clear.

783
00:39:31,677 --> 00:39:33,220
She'll be riding
at Santa Anita next week.

784
00:39:33,345 --> 00:39:36,682
Excellent, and Holwell will soon be
riding a bunk in San Quentin.

785
00:39:36,891 --> 00:39:39,435
Well, I vote whoever won
at the track pays for pizza.

786
00:39:39,643 --> 00:39:41,604
The results were thrown out.
Jane didn't win anything.

787
00:39:41,771 --> 00:39:43,397
Nah, he's still got the money
from the trifecta...

788
00:39:43,522 --> 00:39:44,565
the one, two, three.

789
00:39:44,732 --> 00:39:46,066
Well, uh, not so much.

790
00:39:46,317 --> 00:39:48,194
It cost a lot to, uh, win that.

791
00:39:48,319 --> 00:39:49,779
I had to cover
every 3-way combination

792
00:39:49,904 --> 00:39:52,406
of every horse in the race.
Cost me $5,000

793
00:39:52,823 --> 00:39:54,575
and I only won $486.

794
00:39:54,867 --> 00:39:55,910
Wait a minute.

795
00:39:56,160 --> 00:39:58,287
So... you can't read horses?

796
00:39:58,454 --> 00:40:00,372
Of course not.
But it's always a good idea

797
00:40:00,498 --> 00:40:02,416
to seem like you know
what you're talking about.

798
00:40:02,833 --> 00:40:03,876
Fosters trust.

799
00:40:04,210 --> 00:40:06,128
So that means you put Grace
on a potentially wild horse

800
00:40:06,253 --> 00:40:07,546
with no idea what could happen?

801
00:40:08,172 --> 00:40:09,215
Well, I had an idea

802
00:40:09,340 --> 00:40:11,217
that Holwell was putting a burr
under the saddle.

803
00:40:11,342 --> 00:40:12,635
Very old school trick.

804
00:40:12,760 --> 00:40:15,137
Very old school. That's why
I had Grace ride bareback...

805
00:40:15,262 --> 00:40:17,014
to see if I was right
and I was.

806
00:40:17,264 --> 00:40:18,808
You took a terrible chance.

807
00:40:19,642 --> 00:40:21,644
Well, I figured the odds
were 70-30.

808
00:40:21,769 --> 00:40:23,562
I was right.
I wouldn't call that terrible.

809
00:40:23,687 --> 00:40:26,440
A betting man'd call that risky
but certainly not terrible.

810
00:40:27,191 --> 00:40:28,234
Well...

811
00:40:29,193 --> 00:40:30,611
So... pizza.

812
00:40:38,577 --> 00:40:39,620
Nope.

